    summary: "The hybrid capture HPV test sits under PMA P890064, first approved on 11 March 1991 as the ViraType HPV DNA typing kit (now held by Qiagen Gaithersburg). The Digene Hybrid Capture 2 (hc2) High-Risk HPV DNA Test was approved on 31 March 2003 (supplement S009) for two uses: to screen patients with ASCUS Pap results to decide on referral to colposcopy, and \"in women 30 years and older\" to be used \"with Pap to adjunctively screen to assess the presence or absence of high-risk HPV types\".",
